Subject: Restrict legacy wide-string fallbacks to old MSVC
Upstream: https://github.com/intel/libvpl/pull/198
Commit: 9cb2dc5643480bde33909e11b0ec1ddeb6339f45

MinGW provides wcscpy_s and wcscat_s. Since _MSC_VER is undefined there,
the old condition wrongly enables statement macros that break expressions
in newer mingw-w64 stralign.h. Backport the upstream compiler guard.

diff --git a/libvpl/src/windows/mfx_dispatcher_defs.h b/libvpl/src/windows/mfx_dispatcher_defs.h
--- a/libvpl/src/windows/mfx_dispatcher_defs.h
+++ b/libvpl/src/windows/mfx_dispatcher_defs.h
@@ -20,4 +20,4 @@
-#if _MSC_VER < 1400
+#if defined(_MSC_VER) && _MSC_VER < 1400
     #define wcscpy_s(to, to_size, from) \
         (void)(to_size);                \
         wcscpy(to, from)
